# .env.release.example
#
# Copy to `.env.release` (gitignored) and fill in to enable the Discord release
# announcement that `make release` posts to the shared ZeroSignal #releases
# channel. `make release` auto-sources `.env.release` if it exists.
#
#   cp .env.release.example .env.release   # then edit .env.release
#
# Both values are the two halves of the channel webhook URL
#   https://discord.com/api/webhooks/<ID>/<TOKEN>
# (Discord: Channel -> Integrations -> Webhooks -> New Webhook). Leave either
# blank and the announce is silently skipped; the rest of the release is
# unchanged. zs-node posts to the SAME webhook — the embed author line
# distinguishes them.

DISCORD_WEBHOOK_ID=
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# --- Alternative: keep NO plaintext on disk (macOS Keychain) ---------------
# Store the two halves once (same Keychain zs-proxy's wallet uses):
#   security add-generic-password -U -a "$USER" -s zs-discord-webhook-id    -w '<ID>'
#   security add-generic-password -U -a "$USER" -s zs-discord-webhook-token -w '<TOKEN>'
# Then replace the two assignments above with these, so the file holds no secret:
#   DISCORD_WEBHOOK_ID="$(security find-generic-password -a "$USER" -s zs-discord-webhook-id -w)"
#   DISCORD_WEBHOOK_TOKEN="$(security find-generic-password -a "$USER" -s zs-discord-webhook-token -w)"
